Form 656 — Offer in Compromise
The taxpayer submits an offer in compromise to settle tax debt for less than the full amount owed.
Doubt as to collectibility is the most common basis for an offer in compromise.
The Reasonable Collection Potential (RCP) determines the minimum acceptable offer amount.
RCP = Future Income + Net Equity in Assets.
Application fee: $205 (waivable for low-income taxpayers).
Initial payment: 20% of lump sum offer or first monthly payment for periodic payment offers.
